          "say": "Stage two adds gradients to the sharded categories. Each rank keeps the full parameter set while gradient and optimizer state are partitioned.",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 9.76,
          "duration": 9.36,
          "until": 10.31
        },
        {
          "say": "The ledger now keeps full weights and one quarter of each other category per rank. State memory falls further while model parameters remain replicated.",
          "start": 10.31,
          "end": 19.358,
          "duration": 9.048,
          "until": 19.908
        },
        {
          "say": "Gradient communication now has a sharded output contract. An all-reduce returns the full gradient to every rank, while reduce-scatter sums contributions and leaves each rank its portion. After local optimizer-partition updates, updated parameter slices are shared, for example by all-gather, so every rank again has complete compute weights. Stage one also has to synchronize updated slices; its storage policy alone does not fix the exact runtime collective schedule.",
